# Framer Content Editing Protocol

This is a Framer-exported static site using React hydration. Visible content (text, images, links, `src`/`srcSet`, etc.) is duplicated across **HTML and `.mjs` bundles**. If only HTML is updated, **hydration overwrites** the change with values from JS.

## Goal

Edits must **persist after the full load + hydration cycle**. That requires updating **every** duplicate of the changed string or asset path.

## Workflow (mandatory)

1. **Search the entire repo** for the exact string or path being changed (`*.html`, `*.mjs`, `*.json`). Assume multiple files until proven otherwise.
2. **Update all occurrences** in:
   - **HTML:** the page’s `.html` for page-specific content; **every** `.html` for shared UI (nav, footer, etc.).
   - **`.mjs`:** every chunk that contains the value. Use **replace_all** per file when the minifier repeated it (breakpoints/variants). Check **`shared-lib.DjhlsekC.mjs`** for shared components; check the page chunk from `script_main.ChSf-xMO.mjs` for route-specific content.
   - **`assets/searchIndex.json`:** update each affected route entry when the changed text appears there.
3. **Verify:** search again for the **old** string/path — **zero** results in HTML, MJS, and JSON (unless intentionally kept elsewhere).

## Route → chunk mapping

- Read `routeId` from `data-framer-hydrate-v2` on `<div id="main">` in the HTML.
- In `script_main.ChSf-xMO.mjs`, look up that `routeId` and note the dynamic `import(\`./….mjs\`)` for the page bundle.
- Still **grep the whole repo**; do not edit only one bundle without searching.

## Images and assets

- Update **main** image path **and** all **`srcset` / `srcSet`** variants (e.g. `*_79.jpg`) in **both** HTML and every `.mjs` that references them.
- Update `searchIndex.json` if the asset path appears there.

## Pitfalls

- **Never replace only a URL prefix** (e.g. `https://framer.com/`) when the full value is built as `https://framer.com/@handle` or similar — you can produce invalid URLs like `https://newsite@handle` and break hydration expectations.
- **Breakpoint duplicates:** the same copy or URL may appear many times in one `.mjs` file; use replace_all.
- **Page overrides:** some pages embed their own copy of shared nav/links; always grep, not only `shared-lib`.
